# Week 5 – Model Development & Training

## Objective
The objective of this week is to develop multiple regression models for crop yield prediction and train them using the processed dataset.

## Models Implemented
The following regression models were implemented and trained:

1. Linear Regression  
2. Random Forest Regressor  
3. XGBoost Regressor  

These models were selected to compare both traditional and ensemble learning approaches.

## Model Training
- The dataset was split into training and testing sets.
- Feature-scaled data was used where required.
- Hyperparameters were tuned to improve model performance.

## Model Interpretation
To understand model behavior and feature influence:
- Feature importance was extracted for Random Forest and XGBoost models.
- SHAP (SHapley Additive exPlanations) values were used to interpret the contribution of each feature to crop yield prediction.

## Outcome of Week 5
- Multiple regression models were successfully trained.
- Feature importance and SHAP analysis provided insights into model decision-making.
- Models were prepared for evaluation in the next phase.
